# 2. UNDERSTAND THE MAIN OBJECTIVE

The system must make work easier for every employee.

A cashier needs fast billing.

A stock controller needs accurate inventory.

A buyer needs simple purchasing.

An accountant needs reliable financial records.

A branch manager needs operational control.

A director needs departmental oversight.

The CEO and owners need meaningful business intelligence.

No employee should navigate irrelevant modules or perform unnecessary steps.

However, simplicity must never compromise financial accuracy, authorization, stock integrity or operational accountability.

### PRIMARY RULE

**SHOW EACH ROLE WHAT THEY NEED. HIDE IRRELEVANT COMPLEXITY. PROTECT RESTRICTED OPERATIONS.**

Build one coordinated business system with carefully adapted experiences for different roles.

